::ingredients

(white flour) 300g
(egg) 3
(milk) 60cl
(beer) 20cl
(fat choice) = (butter, melted) 30g -OR- (oil, for batter) 3tbsp
(salt)
(oil, for pan)

::equipment

(pan, flat)
(ladle)
(fabric, oiled piece)

::instructions

{batter} = (white flour) + (salt)
{batter} + (egg)
{batter} + (fat choice)
    <mix>
{batter} + (milk) + (beer)
    <mix, adding the liquids slowly> ?= pours fluidly from the ladle
Optional [
    {batter} <rest, 1h>
]
(pan) <oil, with (oil, for pan), using (fabric)>
    <heat> ?= hot before cooking the first crêpe
Repeat [
    {batter} 1 ladle <pour, into (pan), using (ladle)>
        <spread, thinly by following the pan rotation with (ladle)>
        <cook> ?= dried up
        <flip>
    (pan) <oil, with (oil, for pan), using (fabric), frequently>
]
until all batter cooked

::notes

Mix flour, salt, eggs and melted butter or oil in that order to avoid dry flour.

